    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0141" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1191</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-28T17:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 28, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.41 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1961. I learn that Hertling told the Dutch Minister at Berlin in answer to a
                    question that he could riot have spoken otherwise than he did [about] Belgium;
                    that public opinion would not let him promise the liberation of Belgium until
                    promises had been made of the restoration of the German colonies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
